import json,html,pathlib,statistics,math
R=json.load(open('dev/running-experiment-fixture.json')); B=R['baseline']; E=R['experiment']
T=json.load(open('dev/running-experiment-tempo.json')); D=json.load(open('dev/running-experiment-defense.json')); U=json.load(open('dev/running-experiment-unit.json'))
out=[]
def h(s):out.append('<h2>'+html.escape(s)+'</h2>')
def p(s):out.append('<p>'+s+'</p>')
def table(cols,rows):out.append('<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+html.escape(str(c))+'</th>'for c in cols)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(c))+'</td>'for c in row)+'</tr>'for row in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>')
def n(x):return '—'if x is None else f'{x:.3f}'
def pc(x):return '—'if x is None else f'{100*x:.3f}%'
def pp(x):return f'{100*x:+.3f} pp'
def delta(a,b,percent=False):return pp(b-a)if percent else f'{b-a:+.3f}'
p('<strong>Experimental candidate only. Not committed, published or permanently adopted. The production no-sag baseline remains unchanged. No putback-block correction or other balance change was implemented.</strong>')
h('Decision')
p('<strong>Recommendation: KEEP this eligibility correction as the candidate for review.</strong> It eliminates tempo-only Running treatment and Running+PNR while preserving event-driven Running, coach pace, PNR operation, transition threes and defensive differentiation. Scoring falls modestly in the reference fixture; this is not proof that the scoring problem is solved, nor a reason to make another adjustment.')
h('Exact scope and reproduction')
p('Creation seed 61005; 30 teams; 15 players/team; 150 games; game seeds 100000–100149; identical first ten circle-schedule rounds, alternating venues, preseason state reset before each game. Both baseline and candidate were rerun. The retained reference PPG 123.840, pace 102.380, ORtg 120.961125, 2P 56.390769% and 3P 38.004884% matched exactly. The earlier 123.67 fixture was not substituted.')
p('Two small source transformations are applied only in isolated development VMs: add transitionAdvantage to the existing shot context; make layupOptions check context.transitionAdvantage instead of context.transition. The merged transition expression, its short-circuit RNG behavior and its consumers elsewhere remain untouched. No broad transition refactor or separate engine was introduced.')
out.append('<pre>const shotContext = { transition, transitionAdvantage, ... };&#10;// Only the Running Layup variant gate changes:&#10;if (context.transitionAdvantage) return [existingRunningLayupOption];</pre>')
p('The existing option still has +.055 accuracy and .5 block multiplier. Existing event triggers, including every currently eligible DREB and credited steal, remain unchanged. Non-event possessions use the existing weighted non-transition layup options; no replacement variant is forced. The runningLayup shot-selection key remains eligible under the old merged state, but cannot itself grant the Running Layup variant; its existing −.01 key adjustment remains intact.')
h('1. League-wide comparison')
percent={'FG','twoP','threeP','FT','eFG','TS'}
labels={'PPG':'PPG','pace':'Possessions/team/game','ORtg':'ORtg','FG':'FG%','twoP':'2P%','threeP':'3P%','FT':'FT%','eFG':'eFG%','TS':'TS%','FGA':'FGA/team/game','twoPA':'2PA/team/game','threePA':'3PA/team/game','FTA':'FTA/team/game','TOV':'Player-box TOV/team/game','OREB':'OREB/team/game'}
table(['Metric','Baseline','Experiment','Difference'],[[label,(pc if k in percent else n)(B['league'][k]),(pc if k in percent else n)(E['league'][k]),delta(B['league'][k],E['league'][k],k in percent)]for k,label in labels.items()])
p('Shooting percentages are aggregate makes/attempts, not averages of player percentages. eFG=(FGM+.5×3PM)/FGA; TS=points/[2×(FGA+.44×FTA)]. Pace uses the engine’s on-court possession counters divided by five and includes overtime. TOV above sums player box scores; separate team shot-clock violations are not included in this column. This same convention is used for both branches and defense-test turnovers below.')
d=[e['PPG']-b['PPG']for b,e in zip(B['gameMetrics'],E['gameMetrics'])];se=statistics.stdev(d)/math.sqrt(len(d))
p(f'Paired game-level PPG difference is {statistics.mean(d):+.3f}, with sample standard error {se:.3f}; a rough normal 95% interval is [{statistics.mean(d)-1.96*se:+.3f}, {statistics.mean(d)+1.96*se:+.3f}]. This is a sensitivity diagnostic over the fixed fixture, not evidence of a guaranteed league-wide reduction. Changed variants/outcomes alter later RNG consumption.')
h('2. Running eligibility — required checks')
table(['Metric','Baseline','Experiment'],[['Primary Running evaluations',B['running']['evaluations'],E['running']['evaluations']],['Running evaluations/team/game',n(B['running']['evaluationsPerTeamGame']),n(E['running']['evaluationsPerTeamGame'])],['Running FGA/team/game',n(B['running']['FGAperTeamGame']),n(E['running']['FGAperTeamGame'])],['Share of primary rim evaluations',pc(B['running']['evalShare']),pc(E['running']['evalShare'])],['Share of primary rim FGA',pc(B['running']['FGAShare']),pc(E['running']['FGAShare'])],['Tempo-only Running, primary',B['running']['origins']['coach tempo']['evaluations'],E['running']['origins'].get('coach tempo',{}).get('evaluations',0)],['Tempo-only Running, all paths',B['running']['allPathOrigins']['coach tempo']['evaluations'],E['running']['allPathOrigins'].get('coach tempo',{}).get('evaluations',0)],['Event-derived Running, primary',sum(v['evaluations']for k,v in B['running']['origins'].items()if k!='coach tempo'),sum(v['evaluations']for k,v in E['running']['origins'].items()if k!='coach tempo')],['Running + PNR evaluations',B['PNR']['runningEvaluations'],E['PNR']['runningEvaluations']]])
p('PASS: every experimental Running Layup in the reference, tempo and defense batches had event-derived transitionAdvantage. There were no tempo-only or PNR Running exceptions, including recursive paths. Event-derived count changes from 759 to 761 as downstream trajectories diverge; event-source rules were not edited.')
h('3. Primary rim efficiency')
table(['Metric','Baseline','Experiment','Difference'],[[k,pc(B['primaryRim'][field]),pc(E['primaryRim'][field]),pp(E['primaryRim'][field]-B['primaryRim'][field])]for k,field in [('Observed FG%','FG'),('Base + physical probability','base'),('Context-adjusted probability','context'),('Final probability, all evaluations','probability'),('Final probability, recorded FGA subset','recordedProbability'),('Net context increase','contextDelta')]])
p('Evaluation means include shooting-foul misses that are not recorded as FGA. Final probability includes the actual foul branch, sliders, clamps and home court; it is conditional on no block and is not observed FG%. Context is before the later foul/sliders stages. Primary rim excludes immediate putbacks, recursive attempts and floaters. Its context increase falls from +4.481 to +3.326 pp (−1.155 pp).')
h('4. Variant mix and observed conversion')
names=['Running Layup','Driving Layup','Cutting Layup','Finger Roll Layup','Scoop Layup','Eurostep Layup','Reverse Layup']
table(['Primary rim variant','Baseline FGA','Share of rim','FG%','Experiment FGA','Share of rim','FG%','FG change'],[[k,B['variants'][k]['FGA'],pc(B['variants'][k]['FGA']/B['primaryRim']['FGA']),pc(B['variants'][k]['FG']),E['variants'][k]['FGA'],pc(E['variants'][k]['FGA']/E['primaryRim']['FGA']),pc(E['variants'][k]['FG']),pp(E['variants'][k]['FG']-B['variants'][k]['FG'])]for k in names])
p('All six existing non-Running variants gain aggregate attempts. These are distributions from two full simulations, not one-to-one replacements of particular baseline shots after RNG divergence. Eligible players can also select the existing floater option against high rim defense. Primary floaters increase from 1,641 to 1,767 FGA and are excluded from the rim-variant share denominator above.')
table(['Floater selection key, primary','Baseline FGA','Experiment FGA'],[[k,B['floaterVariants'].get(k,{}).get('FGA',0),E['floaterVariants'].get(k,{}).get('FGA',0)]for k in sorted(set(B['floaterVariants'])|set(E['floaterVariants']))])
p('Largest individual variant swing: Reverse Layup falls from 73.50% (117 FGA) to 66.67% (156 FGA). Its formula is unchanged; these small, differently selected samples do not isolate a Reverse-specific effect. No attempt was made to compensate for this variation.')
h('5. PNR remains functional')
pnrfields=[('Root possessions containing PNR','rootPossessions'),('PNR action calls, including repeats','actionCalls'),('PNR shot evaluations','shotEvaluations'),('Screen boost applications, all primary PNR shots','screenBoostEvaluations'),('Screen boost applications, primary rim only','rimScreenBoostEvaluations'),('Running + PNR evaluations','runningEvaluations')]
table(['Metric','Baseline','Experiment'],[[label,B['PNR'][key],E['PNR'][key]]for label,key in pnrfields]+[['Primary PNR rim FGA',B['PNR']['rim']['FGA'],E['PNR']['rim']['FGA']],['Uncontested PNR rim FGA',B['PNR']['uncontestedRim']['FGA'],E['PNR']['uncontestedRim']['FGA']],['PNR rim FG%',pc(B['PNR']['rim']['FG']),pc(E['PNR']['rim']['FG'])],['PNR root-possession PPP',n(B['PNR']['PPP']),n(E['PNR']['PPP'])]])
p('PNR initiation, screen/recovery logic, coverage, bonuses and open-look behavior were not changed. Rim efficiency decreases when the erroneous Running treatment disappears; this is the intended consequence of the gate, not an edit to PNR bonuses. Overall PNR root-possession PPP remains 1.333→1.337. PPP counts all points in a root possession containing at least one PNR, including free throws and later second chances; it is not a separately isolated single-action play-type statistic.')
h('6. Matched coach-tempo controls')
p('100 games per group and per branch; first 100 reference matchups, seeds 100000–100099, identical copied preseason state. Only temporary coach tempo is 20/50/80. Both baseline control groups reproduce the retained audit exactly. Event/tempo-only rates below use shot evaluations reaching the late transition decision, not all root possessions.')
rows=[]
for r in T:
 for branch in ['baseline','experiment']:
  b=r[branch];rows.append([r['setting'],branch,n(b['league']['pace']),pc(b['transition']['eventRate']),pc(b['transition']['tempoOnlyRate']),n(b['running']['evaluationsPerTeamGame']),pc(b['running']['evalShare']),pc(b['running']['FGAShare']),pc(b['primaryRim']['FG']),pc(b['league']['twoP']),n(b['league']['PPG']),n(b['league']['ORtg'])])
table(['Tempo','Branch','Pace','Event rate','Tempo-only state','Running eval/team/G','Running/rim eval','Running/rim FGA','Rim FG','2P','PPG','ORtg'],rows)
p('PASS: candidate pace rises 94.57→100.07→106.17. The tempo-only state still exists and rises 4.77%→12.06%→19.27%, but generates zero Running variants. Running evaluations/team/game are 2.455→2.530→2.415 instead of the baseline 3.125→3.865→4.805. Event availability, early-three choices and number of possessions can still affect Running counts indirectly; counts are not required to be identical across tempos.')
p('Small within-group pace changes of +.20/+.10/+.10 arise from overtime divergence, not a pace-formula edit: changed game-level possession totals are exactly ±10, matching the existing five-minute overtime at two possessions/minute. At tempo 20 two games add an overtime; at 50 one adds; at 80 two add and one loses an overtime. The reference aggregate pace is unchanged. PPG is not uniformly lower in the controls: tempo 50 rises 119.535→120.720; this is reported rather than adjusted away.')
h('7. Remaining event-derived Running')
table(['Event origin, experiment','Evaluations','FGA','FG%','Final P, evaluations','Final P, FGA subset','Block/FGA'],[[k,v['evaluations'],v['FGA'],pc(v['FG']),pc(v['probability']),pc(v['recordedProbability']),pc(v['blockRate'])]for k,v in E['running']['origins'].items()])
p('All five existing sources remain represented. This experiment does not require a long rebound, unsettled defense or early clock; broad DREB eligibility and late event-derived Running remain separate diagnostic questions.')
h('8. Transition-three preservation')
table(['Metric','Baseline','Experiment'],[[label,B['transitionThrees'][key],E['transitionThrees'][key]]for label,key in [('Early-three FGA','early'),('Other running-three FGA','other'),('Total transition-labelled 3PA','total'),('Tempo-only transition-labelled 3PA','tempoOnly')]]+[['Transition 3P%',pc(B['transitionThrees']['FG']),pc(E['transitionThrees']['FG'])]])
p('No direct changes to early-three or running-three pathways. All 24 isolated three-point construction parity tests passed across merged/event/early flags and three/runningThree/pullupThree keys, using reset RNG. Shot-selection weights also match. Aggregate differences are downstream state/RNG effects, not a removal of the pathway. Tempo-only running threes remain available, as requested.')
h('9. Defensive differentiation')
p('The older defense harness was not present in the retained workspace, so these are fresh matched controls, not claimed reproductions of earlier 102.40/117.98/130.89 values. Each group runs 100 games/branch, same seeds 100000–100099, alternating home/away between fixture teams 0 and 29. Both teams’ base attributes are 75 and tendencies 50; only team 29 perimeter defense, rim defense, defensive IQ, steals and blocks become 60/75/90. Other fixture traits, builds, coaches and league context are preserved across comparisons. Offense measured is team 0 against the controlled defense.')
table(['Defense','Branch','OPPG','Opp FG','Opp 2P','Opp 3P','Opp eFG','Opp PPP','Player TOV forced'],[[r['setting'],branch,n(r[branch]['defense']['OPPG']),pc(r[branch]['defense']['FG']),pc(r[branch]['defense']['twoP']),pc(r[branch]['defense']['threeP']),pc(r[branch]['defense']['eFG']),n(r[branch]['defense']['PPP']),n(r[branch]['defense']['TOVforced'])]for r in D for branch in ['baseline','experiment']])
p('PRESERVED: candidate poor→elite defense lowers OPPG 130.93→108.38 and PPP 1.243→1.033, with more turnovers forced. Defense is not flattened by the Running eligibility change. Nothing in this experiment changes defensive attributes outside these disposable diagnostic fixtures.')
h('10. Finishing-rating differentiation')
p('Actual-engine fixed-probability controls: vary only layup rating, hold other attributes and defender at 75, same build/action, uncontested, neutral home court, block tendency 50%. Event-derived Running retains its original +.055/.5 treatment. Both conversion curves increase strictly with finishing rating.')
table(['Layup rating','Variant','Make probability','Block risk','Expected non-foul conversion'],[[r['rating'],r['variant'],pc(r['probability']),pc(r['blockRisk']),pc(r['expectedNonFoulFG'])]for r in U['curves']])
h('11. Two-point categories')
table(['Category','Primary baseline FGA','Primary baseline FG','Primary experimental FGA','Primary experimental FG','Primary FG change','All-path baseline FG','All-path experimental FG'],[[k,B['primaryCategories'][k]['FGA'],pc(B['primaryCategories'][k]['FG']),E['primaryCategories'][k]['FGA'],pc(E['primaryCategories'][k]['FG']),pp(E['primaryCategories'][k]['FG']-B['primaryCategories'][k]['FG']),pc(B['categories'][k]['FG']),pc(E['categories'][k]['FG'])]for k in ['rim','dunk','floater','midrange','post']])
p('The largest primary category decrease is rim/layup (−1.49 pp). Primary floaters decrease 1.20 pp with a changed eligible mix; dunk, midrange and post change −.66, −.62 and −1.09 pp. None of those probability formulas were edited. Aggregate changes outside rim are not separable from selection and downstream RNG in this single fixture; they are not evidence that an additional correction is needed. Post includes post-skill attempts; midrange excludes those to keep categories disjoint.')
h('12. Putback system — unchanged')
table(['Metric','Baseline','Experiment'],[['Putback attempts/team/game',n(B['putbacks']['perTeamGame']),n(E['putbacks']['perTeamGame'])],['Putback attempts/game, both teams',n(B['putbacks']['perTeamGame']*2),n(E['putbacks']['perTeamGame']*2)],['Putback FG%',pc(B['putbacks']['FG']),pc(E['putbacks']['FG'])],['Layup-putback FGA',B['putbacks']['layups']['FGA'],E['putbacks']['layups']['FGA']],['Layup-putback block rate',pc(B['putbacks']['layups']['blockRate']),pc(E['putbacks']['layups']['blockRate'])]])
p('Immediate putback resolution was not touched. Layup-putback block rate remains exactly zero in both branches. Slight changes in volume/FG reflect changed game trajectories, not implementation of the deferred putback experiment.')
h('Validation, limitations and next decision')
p('150 baseline and 150 candidate reference games each passed instrumented-versus-uninstrumented full-result and complete post-game-state parity. Three pairs/group in all tempo and defense controls also passed (336 total game/state parity checks). FGA and score accounting were checked in every simulated branch. Every candidate shot sample in every batch passed event-origin and no-Running+PNR assertions. No-sag production source and all dist files remain unchanged. No git commit or publish was performed.')
p('Eligible variant selection now matches the requested semantics. Preserve this as the candidate; review these results before authorizing adoption. Do not tune Running accuracy, blocks, PNR or other systems to chase a scoring target. Broader event eligibility, late-clock transition persistence and the separate putback issue remain outside this experiment.')
p('Development files: dev/running-eligibility-candidate.cjs, dev/experiment-running.cjs, dev/test-running-eligibility.cjs, dev/report-running-experiment.py and the four running-experiment-*.json results. Reproduce from the repository with: node dev/experiment-running.cjs fixture 150; node dev/experiment-running.cjs tempo 100; node dev/experiment-running.cjs defense 100; node dev/test-running-eligibility.cjs; python3 dev/report-running-experiment.py. Production reference remains commit 2748e11d3205246762bdd68e001a9f0495551ae9.')
out.append('<details><summary>Complete machine-readable results</summary><pre>'+html.escape(json.dumps({'fixture':R,'tempo':T,'defense':D,'unit':U},indent=2))+'</pre></details>')
